114. OUTLINES OF JAINISM

Seven kinds, which are viruddha, viz. according as the
(positive) middle term is:

1. svabhitva, property of major: no cold by heat;
2. vyapya: no quiescence by anger ;
3. kdrya: no cold by smoke ;
4, kérana: no happiness in the world by soul is
impure ;
5. pirva- ~cheure : no sunset by daylight ;
6. uitara-chara: no daylight by sunset ;
7, saha-chara: no not-sweet by yellow-ripe mango.

Anupalabdhi
also has sub-kinds: aviruddha and viruddha.

Seven aviruddha kinds, viz. according as the ( negative }
middle term is:

1. svabhdva : no jug here, because none is visible:
2. vyapaka: no mango-tree, because no tree ;
3. karya: no good seed, because no sprout ;
4, karana : no smoke, because no fire ;
5. piirva-chara: no rise of Rohint (constellation) in
two ghatis, because Krittikd has not risen now;
6. witara-chara: no vise of Bharant two ghatis ago.
because Krittika has not risen now : :
7. saha-chara: no rise in one scale e-pan, because there
is no lowering of the other.

Five Viruddha-anupalabdhis (with negative middle):
1. svabhdva: things are many-sided, because we
cannot get a purely one-sided thing ;
2. vydpuka: shade by no heat :

